From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: comdlg32, shell32, explorerframe: the file dialogs as Windows shows them

David: the common dialogs (Open picture etc.) "look old/grey". GetOpenFileName
and GetSaveFileName showed the "Look in" dialog of Windows 2000 even with no
hook or template, and the item dialog (IFileOpenDialog) was grey with
comctl32's old toolbar bitmaps, no address and a tree of Internet Explorer's
Favorites and the whole desktop.

- comdlg32: as Windows since Vista, GetOpenFileName/GetSaveFileName with no
  hook and no template (ANSI or Unicode) show the item dialog: filters,
  title, default extension, first folder and name, and the flags carried
  over; the result written back in the caller's form (one path, or "folder\0
  name\0...\0\0" for several; offsets, file title, filter index; the size
  needed when the buffer is too small); the working directory changed unless
  OFN_NOCHANGEDIR. HKCU\Software\Stained Glass\FileDialogs ClassicLook=1
  keeps the older dialog.
- comdlg32 item dialog: a white dialog; File Explorer's back, forward and up
  arrows (whole-pixel, as in 0516) instead of the old bitmaps; an address box
  that names the folder and goes where it is told on Enter; a larger default
  size, so the list's columns show.
- shell32 ExplorerBrowser: the folder tree's roots are the user's Desktop,
  Downloads, Documents and Pictures, This PC and Network (Windows' Quick
  access, This PC, Network) instead of IE Favorites and the desktop tree.
- explorerframe: the tree uses the Explorer theme (chevrons, no dotted lines).

Gate: make test-ofn.
